menu "vstreamer"

config VSTREAMER_RS_PIE
    bool "Reed-Solomon FEC encode with the PIE SIMD kernel"
    depends on SOC_CPU_HAS_PIE
    default y
    help
        Encode FEC parity with the ESP32-P4 PIE kernel instead of the table path: about 2.8x
        faster (k=21, 10 parity rows, 1403-byte shards: 2.7 ms vs 7.7 ms), which frees about
        16% of core 0 at FEC 21/31.

        Cost: the hardware H.264 encoder shares PSRAM bandwidth with the FEC path, and the
        faster kernel sends each block's parity in a tighter burst. With fec_spread_ms 0 that
        costs about 1 encoder fps at 21/31 (26.4 vs 27.4); with fec_spread_ms 25 or more the
        difference is about 0.1-0.3 fps. Turn it off where every encoder frame matters more
        than core 0 time.

endmenu
